Operator fusion also depends on repeated, alignable operands. When compatible pairs are rare,
when normalization dominates, or when another representation preserves substantially more sharing,
the CM path may tie or lose. These are expected boundary cases, not failures to be hidden. The
final discussion will interpret them together with preparation cost, memory traffic, reuse count,
variable ordering, and fallback frequency.
10 Conclusion
Correspondence matrices are best understood as typed Boolean operators rather than as a novelty
claim about reshaped truth tables. XOR–AND contraction lets one-hot operand states evaluate
those operators; matrix transformations align signed operand frames; and exact compatible frames
can be fused before evaluation. Formula-valued logical matrices add a symbolic layer whose valuation
recovers numeric CMs and whose logical pairing remains within Boolean algebra. The remaining
empirical question is deliberately practical: which workloads permit this operator-level rewrite to
reduce total computation after all costs are counted?
